<!-- snippets/jc-gallery-thumbs.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  Mobile-only thumbnail strip for the PDP gallery.

  The product template runs media_gallery_style: "grid", which stacks all media
  on desktop and gives a swipeable slider on mobile but ships no thumbnails on
  mobile. This adds them under 768px and leaves desktop untouched, rather than
  switching to "Slider & thumbnails" and rebuilding the desktop layout in CSS.

  MUST BE RENDERED AS A BLOCK INSIDE sections/product__main.liquid.
  galleryScrollToIndex() resolves the slider through $refs.formContainer, and
  x-ref="formContainer" sits on product__main (line 157). Moved into a
  standalone section, $refs.formContainer is undefined and the call throws.
  Do not refactor this into its own section — it breaks silently.

  Three theme behaviours this leans on, all in assets/main-2qOaomAO.js:
  - galleryScrollToIndex(i) is the theme's own Alpine method. Reused rather
    than reimplementing scroll code.
  - That method picks its slider with
    `Array.from(sliders).find((s) => s.offsetWidth > 0)`. product__main renders
    the gallery twice (a md:hidden mobile copy and the desktop column), so this
    automatically targets whichever one is actually visible. No viewport JS
    needed here.
  - The active state binds to gallery_index, which each slide's own
    x-intersect:enter.half keeps in sync in product__gallery-grid.liquid. So the
    active thumb tracks swiping, not just clicks.

  Renders nothing for single-media products.

  It must also be FIRST in the section's block_order. The block's `position`
  setting only controls the desktop column; the mobile branch of product__main
  (line 229) renders every block in plain editor order under the gallery, so
  block_order alone decides whether the strip sits under the gallery or halfway
  down the buy column. Reordering blocks in the theme editor will move it.

  Usage — as a Custom Liquid block in Product main, first in block_order:
    {% render 'jc-gallery-thumbs' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
  {% comment %}
    settings.gap_size is the padding the gallery slider gives itself in
    product__gallery-grid.liquid. Passing it through lets the CSS line the first
    thumbnail up with the image edge above it instead of with the px-4 the
    product__liquid block wrapper adds.
  {% endcomment %}
  <div class="jc-gthumbs" style="--jc-gthumbs-inset: {{ settings.gap_size }}px;">
    {%- for media in product.media -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="jc-gthumbs__item"
        {% comment %}
          Hardcoded English, matching the other jc-* snippets — there is no
          suitable key in locales/en.default.json and the theme's own gallery
          indicators are unlocalised too.
        {% endcomment %}
        aria-label="{% if media.alt != blank %}{{ media.alt | escape }}{% else %}View media {{ forloop.index }} of {{ product.media.size }}{% endif %}"
        @click="galleryScrollToIndex({{ forloop.index0 }});"
        :class="gallery_index === {{ forloop.index0 }} ? 'is-active' : ''"
        :aria-current="gallery_index === {{ forloop.index0 }} ? 'true' : 'false'"
      >
        {%- if media.media_type == 'model' -%}
          <span class="jc-gthumbs__badge">
            {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'box', size: '14' %}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if media.media_type == 'external_video' or media.media_type == 'video' -%}
          <span class="jc-gthumbs__badge">
            {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'play', size: '14' %}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {% comment %}
          enable_scroll_motion: false — component__image otherwise adds
          motion-safe:scroll-blurinzoom-2-20, a view()-timeline animation. In a
          horizontally scrolling strip that resolves against the wrong scroll
          axis and can leave thumbnails stuck mid-animation. Nothing to gain
          from it at 64px anyway.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% render 'component__image',
          image: media,
          max_width: 200,
          ratio_class: 'aspect-[1/1]',
          crop_class: 'object-cover',
          enable_lazy_load: true,
          enable_2x: true,
          enable_scroll_motion: false
        %}
      </button>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
